# English for engineers

This repository may be read by non–Polish-speaking programmers. Keep engineer-facing language in English.

Canonical domain terms live in `docs/application_idea.md` (Terminology). Use those, not Polish UI labels, in:

- Commit titles and messages
- Code comments
- Tests (including `it('...')` titles)
- Documentation (`docs/`, architecture notes, READMEs)
- Identifiers, types, ports, logs aimed at operators/developers

| Prefer (English) | Avoid in non-UI text |
|---|---|
| Companionship | Akompaniament / Akompaniamenty |
| Accompanied | Akompaniowany |
| Companion | Akompaniator |
| Companionship relation | akompaniament (as a row/feature name) |

```text
# ❌ commit / comment / docs
Add Akompaniowany couple options on + Dodaj Akompaniament

# ✅
Add Accompanied couple options on the Add Companionship form
```

**Polish is allowed only in user-visible UI strings** (labels, buttons, form errors shown to the delegate, `aria-label` copy that matches the screen). Do not invent a localization layer until a dedicated i18n story asks for it.

When docs describe a screen, name it in English (route / tab purpose). Do not paste Polish chrome into docs unless you are documenting the exact UI string, and even then prefer English plus the path (`/app/companionships?tab=new`).
